# Cool but Rude, level 1: with no card in hand there is nothing to discard, so "you may discard a card" asks nothing and
# "if you do, draw a card" does not happen. Bot1 plays out its whole hand on turn 1 (five Moxen are free), draws and plays a
# Mountain on turn 3, and attacks with an empty hand: no discard is asked (the refusal; the two scenarios where the hand
# is not empty are its positive controls) and the library keeps all ten of its cards.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Cool but Rude
Ornithopter
Mountain
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cool but Rude.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot2.Life = 20
